  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Livelihoods protection programme for HBC/PLWHA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the livelihoods protection programme is aimed at promoting recovery from a protracted drought to enhance resilience of the affected communities through strengthening and diversification of their livelihood options. 

Rains in Kitui, Kyuso, Mutomo and Mwingi districts have failed miserably in 2008 and the government has declared the current drought a national disaster. The community requires food assistance to set them through the seven month June to December 2009 as a poor season is expected between April and June 2009.</narrative>
  </description>
